On 10/23/07, Yoav Nir <yoav.nir@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> Should it be {lo nu cpare}, or should we use {du'u} or {su'u}?
> I thought that {nu} is specific to events, whereas {su'u} is more general.
> Or is crawling an event/achievement?
>

{nu} refers to events not in the sense of "Eurovision Song Contest" events,
but generally to occurrences, things that happen. You can sometimes be more
specific by using {zu'o}, {za'i}, {mu'e}, {pu'u}.

{su'u} is the most general abstractor; it can pretty much stand in for all
members of NU.

On 10/23/07, Pierre Abbat <phma@phma.optus.nu > wrote:
> >
> > .i la kan,r. cilre lo du'u muvgau lo mokau sluni kei lo nu cpare
>
>
mi na djuno lo smuni be di'u i u'i je ku'i la'a la'e ri xajmi

i mu'o mi'e komfn

